*> End to end test of the chunk feed (core/src/chunk-feed.cob; the join in CHUNKS-INITIAL-BATCH, the move in CHUNKS-FOLLOW, the tick in CORE-TICK): in a world whose chunks are generated by the
*> time-sliced queue (the standard pipeline over core/tests/fixtures/gen) a joining player gets the chunk cache center and no chunk in the join itself; the chunks follow batch by batch
*> as the queue finishes them, nearest first (the chunk of the player's feet before any of the ring around it), at most CF-SENDS per tick, each batch as Chunk Batch Start, chunks,
*> Chunk Batch Finished; every chunk of the view arrives exactly once; a move to the next chunk forgets the far column and feeds the new one without resending the others; a teleport far
*> away feeds the new view; a disconnect stops the feed and loses nothing (the generated chunks stay loaded).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CHUNK-FEED.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY GENSTAGE.
 COPY CLIMATE.
 COPY CBLOCKS.
 COPY CHUNKFEED.
 COPY GENQUEUE.
 01 WS-DIR                 PIC X(1100) VALUE "core/tests/fixtures/gen".
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-J                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM3                BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-LX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MINS.
    05 WS-MIN              BINARY-DOUBLE OCCURS 6 TIMES.
 01 WS-MAXS.
    05 WS-MAX              BINARY-DOUBLE OCCURS 6 TIMES.
 01 WS-OFFSET              BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 0.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(40).
 01 WS-PLAYER-NAME         PIC X(16) VALUE "Feed".
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG VALUE 4.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PLAYER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-CHUNKS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TOTAL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SUM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LAST-SUM            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TICKS               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MAX-PER-TICK        BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BAD                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CENTER-OK           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-POS                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ID                  BINARY-LONG VALUE 31.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-PITCH               FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-FLAGS               BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LOADED-BEFORE       BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FIRST-TICK          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-STEPS-BEFORE        BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-MAX-STEPS           BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 0.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE 1 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE 12345 TO CW-SEED
     MOVE 6 TO CB-BLOCK-COUNT
     MOVE 300 TO CB-STATE-COUNT
     MOVE 11 TO CB-EPOCH
     MOVE "minecraft:air" TO CB-KEY(1)
     MOVE 13 TO CB-KEY-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE 0 TO CB-DEFAULT-STATE(1)
     MOVE "minecraft:stone" TO CB-KEY(2)
     MOVE 15 TO CB-KEY-LENGTH(2)
     MOVE 1 TO CB-DEFAULT-STATE(2)
     MOVE "minecraft:water" TO CB-KEY(3)
     MOVE 15 TO CB-KEY-LENGTH(3)
     MOVE 86 TO CB-DEFAULT-STATE(3)
     MOVE "minecraft:lava" TO CB-KEY(4)
     MOVE 14 TO CB-KEY-LENGTH(4)
     MOVE 102 TO CB-DEFAULT-STATE(4)
     MOVE 2 TO CBI-COUNT
     MOVE "minecraft:plains" TO CBI-KEY(1)
     MOVE 16 TO CBI-KEY-LENGTH(1)
     MOVE "minecraft:desert" TO CBI-KEY(2)
     MOVE 16 TO CBI-KEY-LENGTH(2)
     CALL "CLIMATE-POINTS-RESET"
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 6
         MOVE -10000 TO WS-MIN(WS-I)
         MOVE 10000 TO WS-MAX(WS-I)
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 1399 TO WS-MAX(6)
     MOVE "minecraft:plains" TO WS-NAME
     CALL "CLIMATE-POINT-ADD" USING WS-NAME WS-MINS WS-MAXS WS-OFFSET
     MOVE 10000 TO WS-MAX(6)
     MOVE 1400 TO WS-MIN(6)
     MOVE "minecraft:desert" TO WS-NAME
     CALL "CLIMATE-POINT-ADD" USING WS-NAME WS-MINS WS-MAXS WS-OFFSET
     CALL "WORLDGEN-FREE"
     CALL "NOISES-LOAD" USING WS-DIR WS-STATUS
     CALL "DENSITY-FUNCTIONS-LOAD" USING WS-DIR WS-STATUS
     CALL "GEN-QUEUE-RESET"
     INITIALIZE GEN-STAGES

*>   join: no chunk in the join itself
     CALL "TEST-JOIN-UNDRAINED" USING WS-PLAYER-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-CONN
     MOVE CN-PLAYER(WS-CONN) TO WS-PLAYER
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
*>   the player enters the standard overworld (dimension row 3, generated by the sliced queue): the initial batch of a dimension change
     MOVE 3 TO PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 8.5 TO PL-X(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 250 TO PL-Y(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 8.5 TO PL-Z(WS-PLAYER)
     CALL "CHUNKS-INITIAL-BATCH" USING WS-CONN
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: the initial batch of the overworld sends the center and no chunk (id 46): the chunks come from the queue" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING TL-OBSERVED-N FOR ALL " 46"
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING TL-OBSERVED-N FOR ALL "x46"
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: the feed serves the player (active, view distance 1)" TO TL-CASE
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = CF-ACTIVE(WS-PLAYER) * 10 + CF-D(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 11 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   tick until the whole view of 9 chunks has been sent: nearest first, at most CF-SENDS per tick, each tick's batch whole
     MOVE 0 TO WS-TICKS WS-LAST-SUM WS-MAX-PER-TICK WS-BAD WS-CENTER-OK WS-TOTAL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FIRST-TICK
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-LAST-SUM >= 9 OR WS-TICKS > 4000
         MOVE GQ-STEPS TO WS-STEPS-BEFORE
         CALL "TEST-TICKS-ANSWERED" USING WS-ONE
         ADD 1 TO WS-TICKS
         IF GQ-STEPS - WS-STEPS-BEFORE > WS-MAX-STEPS
             COMPUTE WS-MAX-STEPS = GQ-STEPS - WS-STEPS-BEFORE
         END-IF
         MOVE 0 TO WS-SUM
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 9
             ADD CF-SENT(WS-PLAYER, WS-I) TO WS-SUM
         END-PERFORM
         CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
         IF WS-SUM - WS-LAST-SUM > WS-MAX-PER-TICK
             COMPUTE WS-MAX-PER-TICK = WS-SUM - WS-LAST-SUM
         END-IF
         IF WS-LAST-SUM = 0 AND WS-SUM > 0
             MOVE CF-SENT(WS-PLAYER, 5) TO WS-CENTER-OK
             MOVE WS-TICKS TO WS-FIRST-TICK
         END-IF
         IF WS-SUM > WS-LAST-SUM
             MOVE 0 TO WS-POS
             INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING WS-POS FOR ALL "12"
             IF WS-POS = 0
                 ADD 1 TO WS-BAD
             END-IF
         END-IF
         MOVE WS-SUM TO WS-LAST-SUM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: all nine chunks of the view are sent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-LAST-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 9 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: the first chunk sent is the chunk of the player's feet" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-CENTER-OK TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: at most CF-SENDS chunks are sent in a tick" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-MAX-PER-TICK TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF WS-MAX-PER-TICK > 0 AND WS-MAX-PER-TICK <= CF-SENDS
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: the queue ran at most GQ-STEP-BUDGET generation steps in any tick (the budget is respected)" TO TL-CASE
     IF WS-MAX-STEPS > 0 AND WS-MAX-STEPS <= GQ-STEP-BUDGET
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: every tick that sends a chunk sends it inside a Chunk Batch Start (12)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-BAD TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: the chunks were not generated before the ticks (the queue built them one by one: chunks generated by the queue)" TO TL-CASE
     IF GQ-GENERATED >= 9
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: once the view is complete nothing more is sent (a tick drains nothing)" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-TICKS" USING WS-ID
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING TL-OBSERVED-N FOR ALL "46"
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   a move to the next chunk (x + 16): the far column is forgotten (id 38), the new column fed, the sent ones kept
     MOVE PL-X(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-X
     MOVE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Y
     MOVE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Z
     ADD 16 TO WS-X
     MOVE 31 TO WS-POS
     CALL "TEST-MOVE" USING WS-CONN WS-POS WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-PITCH WS-FLAGS
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: a move to the next chunk sends the center and the forgets of the far column (96, 38x3) and no chunk yet" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING TL-OBSERVED-N FOR ALL "38x3"
     INSPECT WS-TEXT TALLYING TL-OBSERVED-N FOR ALL "46"
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SUM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 9
         ADD CF-SENT(WS-PLAYER, WS-I) TO WS-SUM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: after the move the six chunks of the overlap keep their sent flag and the new column has none" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 6 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-TICKS WS-LAST-SUM
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-LAST-SUM >= 9 OR WS-TICKS > 4000
         CALL "TEST-TICKS-ANSWERED" USING WS-ONE
         ADD 1 TO WS-TICKS
         MOVE 0 TO WS-LAST-SUM
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 9
             ADD CF-SENT(WS-PLAYER, WS-I) TO WS-LAST-SUM
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: the three new chunks arrive and the view is complete again" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-LAST-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 9 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   a teleport far away: the new view is fed from nothing
     CALL "TEST-DRAIN-IDS" USING WS-CONN WS-TEXT
     ADD 4000 TO WS-X
     CALL "TEST-MOVE" USING WS-CONN WS-POS WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-PITCH WS-FLAGS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SUM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 9
         ADD CF-SENT(WS-PLAYER, WS-I) TO WS-SUM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: a teleport 4000 blocks away leaves no chunk of the new view sent" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-TICKS WS-LAST-SUM
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-LAST-SUM >= 9 OR WS-TICKS > 4000
         CALL "TEST-TICKS-ANSWERED" USING WS-ONE
         ADD 1 TO WS-TICKS
         MOVE 0 TO WS-LAST-SUM
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 9
             ADD CF-SENT(WS-PLAYER, WS-I) TO WS-LAST-SUM
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: the view around the teleport target is fed in full" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-LAST-SUM TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 9 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   a light spread that reaches an unloaded neighbour chunk stops there (the sliced dimension never generates it for a light)
     COMPUTE WS-CX = CF-CX(WS-PLAYER) - 1
     COMPUTE WS-CZ = CF-CZ(WS-PLAYER) - 1
     CALL "WORLD-FIND" USING WS-DIM3 WS-CX WS-CZ WS-ROW
     COMPUTE WS-LX = WS-CX * 16
     COMPUTE WS-LZ = WS-CZ * 16
     MOVE 250 TO WS-J
     MOVE 15 TO WS-I
     CALL "LIGHT-SPREAD" USING WS-ROW WS-LX WS-J WS-LZ WS-I
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: a light spread at the edge of the loaded view returns (the unloaded neighbour blocks it)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   a view distance above the feed's limit is clamped; a player who left the fed dimension is not fed
     MOVE 30 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE CORE-SETTINGS TO CW-SETTINGS
     MOVE 5 TO WS-CX
     MOVE 5 TO WS-CZ
     CALL "CHUNK-FEED-RESET" USING WS-PLAYER WS-CX WS-CZ
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: a view distance of 30 is clamped to CF-MAX-D" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE CF-D(WS-PLAYER) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE CF-MAX-D TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE CORE-SETTINGS TO CW-SETTINGS
     MOVE 0 TO CF-ACTIVE(WS-PLAYER)
     CALL "CHUNK-FEED-RESET" USING WS-PLAYER WS-CX WS-CZ
     MOVE 2 TO PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER)
     CALL "TEST-TICKS" USING WS-ONE
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: a player in another dimension than the fed one is skipped" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 3 TO PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER)
*>   a disconnect: the feed stops and the chunks stay loaded
     MOVE GQ-GENERATED TO WS-LOADED-BEFORE
     CALL "CORE-CONN-CLOSED" USING WS-CONN
     MOVE 5 TO WS-ID
     CALL "TEST-TICKS" USING WS-ID
     MOVE "acceptance chunk feed: after the disconnect the feed sends nothing and the ticks go on without error" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE GQ-GENERATED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF GQ-GENERATED >= WS-LOADED-BEFORE
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TEST-CHUNK-FEED.
 COPY CORETEST.
